WEBVTT

00:00.920 --> 00:03.500
<i>The fifth race brought up
long-lost memories.</i>

00:04.090 --> 00:06.670
<i>I recognized Spirit
as the alien responsible</i>

00:06.840 --> 00:08.880
<i>for my mother's death
in her last race.</i>

00:09.130 --> 00:11.050
<i>All I could think of was revenge.</i>

00:11.600 --> 00:12.350
<i>But I was wrong.</i>

00:12.510 --> 00:14.560
<i>Spirit had nothing to do
with my mother's crash.</i>

00:14.810 --> 00:16.100
<i>It was an accident.</i>

00:16.520 --> 00:18.850
<i>And that wasn't the last
of my surprises.</i>

00:19.650 --> 00:22.650
The powers of the Avatar
are limitless.

00:22.940 --> 00:25.150
He can offer the winner anything.

00:29.530 --> 00:30.610
Mommy.

01:53.070 --> 01:54.780
<i>Limitless powers?</i>

01:55.240 --> 01:56.700
<i>Destroying worlds?</i>

01:57.830 --> 02:01.370
<i>Sorry, Don,
but I don't buy a word of it.</i>

02:05.460 --> 02:08.550
<i>Then again, others might.</i>

02:09.300 --> 02:11.130
<i>And that could be dangerous.</i>

02:26.560 --> 02:29.230
<i>Can I really
make you come back, mother?</i>

02:30.780 --> 02:33.450
<i>Can things really be
the way they were?</i>

02:38.660 --> 02:41.120
I wish you would never have left me.

02:54.300 --> 02:56.640
Any news from Stan and Koji?

02:57.640 --> 02:59.140
Uh, nothing.

03:02.350 --> 03:04.020
We still have some time.

03:04.310 --> 03:05.770
We don't race till tomorrow.

03:06.100 --> 03:08.900
They'll find the spare parts we need.
I'm sure of it.

03:09.150 --> 03:11.400
The Arrow 2 will be as good as new.

03:12.150 --> 03:15.700
Your optimism is commendable,
but I find that unlikely.

03:31.130 --> 03:32.800
Tell me you found something.

03:33.300 --> 03:37.470
A couple of aluminum plates,
some engine fluid, a few tools.

03:37.840 --> 03:40.180
I got nothing. And you?

03:41.390 --> 03:41.930
Ditto.

03:51.190 --> 03:53.610
Hey, look.
The local heroes.

03:55.070 --> 03:56.700
You mean the Scrub pilots?

03:57.450 --> 04:00.200
If anyone knows about parts,
it's gotta be those guys.

04:00.370 --> 04:01.030
I don't think that's a good...

04:01.200 --> 04:02.580
-Come on.
-Koji! Wait a sec.

04:06.160 --> 04:07.250
Well, hello there.

04:08.460 --> 04:09.420
Flint.

04:09.580 --> 04:11.500
It's our good friends from Earth.

04:11.750 --> 04:14.590
Well, well, well.
What a pleasant surprise.

04:14.760 --> 04:16.840
The team that humiliated us

04:17.170 --> 04:19.380
in front of our loving home crowd.

04:20.050 --> 04:21.430
Yeah, I guess that's us.

04:22.470 --> 04:25.220
You think you can barge in here
and make a calamari stew

04:25.390 --> 04:26.430
just like that?

04:30.980 --> 04:33.860
-We were looking for...
-We'll leave you two in peace.

04:34.020 --> 04:35.610
Bad idea.

04:36.190 --> 04:38.650
Hold it right there, boys.

04:39.570 --> 04:41.450
So you think Scrubs
have no pride?

04:41.870 --> 04:42.780
Is that it?

04:47.660 --> 04:50.250
You Earth people have a lot
of nerve, but that's about it.

04:55.800 --> 04:57.340
OK. Run!

05:05.810 --> 05:07.060
Koji, hurry up!

05:24.320 --> 05:25.910
Leave us alone!

05:30.210 --> 05:31.210
Stan!

05:41.510 --> 05:43.680
Well, well, well.
Hold it, my darlings.

05:43.840 --> 05:45.300
Don't eat them just yet.

05:45.600 --> 05:46.560
OK, humans.

05:46.720 --> 05:48.270
What have you got to say
for yourselves?

05:48.770 --> 05:51.640
We're very sorry.
We meant no harm, OK?

05:51.850 --> 05:53.350
Our star-racer is trashed,

05:53.520 --> 05:55.480
and we're looking
for parts to fix it. That's all.

05:59.480 --> 06:01.360
Parts? Are you crazy?

06:01.530 --> 06:02.570
This is Alwas.

06:02.740 --> 06:04.910
Our people have yet
to discover fire.

06:08.450 --> 06:10.290
There just may be an alternative.

06:11.450 --> 06:13.290
Hey,FHnt
What are you talking about?

06:13.460 --> 06:14.790
We're not going to help them.

06:15.080 --> 06:16.210
I forbid it.

06:17.090 --> 06:19.670
Can't you see
this is our big chance?

06:19.840 --> 06:22.670
If this team makes it to Oban,
then we've been beaten

06:22.840 --> 06:24.720
by the best there is.

06:27.760 --> 06:30.970
Of course we will have lost,
but we will have lost with honor.

06:31.310 --> 06:33.350
Our people will love us again.

06:33.980 --> 06:35.400
That's a good point.

06:37.810 --> 06:39.520
OK, humans. Let's go.

06:41.190 --> 06:43.030
Time to make us famous.

06:43.950 --> 06:46.450
Uh, but what about the worms?

06:46.620 --> 06:47.740
They're caterpillars.

06:47.910 --> 06:49.660
Unless you're seaweed,
they won't eat you.

06:58.880 --> 07:01.760
There's one thing
I got to do before I leave.

07:13.270 --> 07:16.020
There's nothing broken
I hope, Miss Wei.

07:16.310 --> 07:18.650
I... well...

07:18.810 --> 07:20.820
You're Don Wei's daughter,
aren't you?

07:21.400 --> 07:24.190
Yes, that's me.
But how did you find out?

07:27.910 --> 07:29.530
Pilot's intuition.

07:30.830 --> 07:33.540
It all came clear
during your race against Spirit.

07:33.910 --> 07:35.290
Does he know?

07:36.290 --> 07:39.790
I didn't say anything to Don,
but I really think you should.

07:43.250 --> 07:44.840
It's not as easy as that.

07:45.010 --> 07:46.760
I don't know if I'm ready
to face him yet.

07:49.010 --> 07:51.470
Look, I'm sure you've got
plenty of reasons

07:51.640 --> 07:53.770
to pretend you're someone else
with your father.

07:53.930 --> 07:55.560
Hey, that's your thing.

07:55.730 --> 07:58.600
But you've got to deal
with your demons.

07:59.190 --> 08:04.610
Otherwise, you'll never grow,
as a pilot or as a person.

08:04.820 --> 08:06.400
I'll try.

08:06.570 --> 08:08.070
But I can't promise anything.

08:09.280 --> 08:11.200
That's all I wanted to hear.

08:15.700 --> 08:17.120
Uh, Rick?

08:18.290 --> 08:19.500
Thank you.

08:24.250 --> 08:27.220
-Where are they taking us?
-Come on, humans. Hurry up!

08:33.560 --> 08:34.810
It's this way.

08:36.180 --> 08:38.480
Stan, I don't like
the look of this.

08:40.600 --> 08:42.730
I think this is where
they dump the bodies.

08:42.900 --> 08:44.820
-What?
-Come on, humans.

08:44.980 --> 08:47.610
We've got parts to find.
Get the lead out!

09:08.010 --> 09:10.590
-Dead end.
-I knew it. It's a trap.

09:11.260 --> 09:12.890
This is your last stop, boys.

09:13.050 --> 09:14.970
Yeah, it's straight down from here.

09:16.140 --> 09:18.310
Stan, I've always
admired your work.

09:18.480 --> 09:19.680
You were a great mechanic.

09:21.520 --> 09:24.610
At my signal, run.
I'll cover you.

09:24.770 --> 09:26.900
No, this was my fault.
I'll cover you.

09:33.070 --> 09:34.410
Oh, wow.

09:37.870 --> 09:40.000
The star-racer graveyard.

09:43.040 --> 09:44.420
This way, humans.

09:48.050 --> 09:50.550
So this is where
the lost ships go?

09:51.090 --> 09:54.640
The Scrub elders strictly forbid
the use of technology,

09:54.800 --> 09:56.810
but they know it comes in handy.

09:57.350 --> 10:00.430
They let us do our thing
as long as they don't have to see it.

10:04.190 --> 10:06.520
You know,
we built our star-racer.

10:28.500 --> 10:29.630
Here goes nothing.

10:32.090 --> 10:33.680
Good morning, sir.

10:38.760 --> 10:40.770
Sir, there's something
I have to tell you.

10:42.310 --> 10:44.770
Excellent, because there's
something I have to tell you.

10:46.980 --> 10:50.860
Our relationship has always been
rather tense, wouldn't you say?

10:51.190 --> 10:53.110
That's a pretty
accurate assessment, sir.

10:53.320 --> 10:55.450
It hasn't been easy.
But I must say...

10:55.660 --> 10:57.490
The pressure of the race
doesn't fully

10:57.660 --> 10:59.580
explain the problem, Molly.

11:02.500 --> 11:04.790
I'm sorry.
I'm not sure I follow.

11:08.130 --> 11:10.590
Back on Earth,
I have a daughter.

11:13.510 --> 11:16.090
She must be
about the same age as you now.

11:16.430 --> 11:19.300
I'm afraid I've transferred
some of my personal problems

11:19.470 --> 11:21.720
with her onto you
and I regret this.

11:23.060 --> 11:23.810
Oh, really?

11:23.980 --> 11:26.140
What sort of problems
did you have with your daughter?

11:27.770 --> 11:29.900
It's, uh, a difficult story.

11:30.480 --> 11:34.490
Let's just say I wasn't able
to see her as much as I wished.

11:36.030 --> 11:36.700
What?

11:38.450 --> 11:41.160
Is that all you have to say?
What are you gonna do about it?

11:41.330 --> 11:42.990
Are you going to see her
when you're back on Earth?

11:44.290 --> 11:45.620
I don't really know.

11:45.790 --> 11:48.880
We've been apart for so long.
I'm afraid it's too late now.

11:49.460 --> 11:52.670
In life, missed opportunities
never return.

11:58.010 --> 12:00.640
As I said, I apologize.

12:01.890 --> 12:04.100
Now, Molly, what was it
you wanted to tell me?

12:05.310 --> 12:06.730
Absolutely nothing!

12:09.650 --> 12:12.020
You may be
a great team manager.

12:12.230 --> 12:14.230
But as a father,
you're clearly a zero.

12:14.940 --> 12:16.990
Molly, it's
far more complex than you...

12:17.320 --> 12:20.240
If I was your daughter,
I'd never want to see you again.

12:21.030 --> 12:22.330
Come back here.

12:28.040 --> 12:29.620
Hey, Molly. Wait up.

12:35.590 --> 12:36.630
What's your problem?

12:38.130 --> 12:41.090
Oh, I bet you got another lecture
from Don Wei. Is that it?

12:41.260 --> 12:43.350
I'd rather not talk about it.
Thank you.

12:48.140 --> 12:52.690
We now call forth Rush
from planet Byrus

12:53.060 --> 12:57.440
and Toros,
colonel of the Crog lmperium.

13:05.950 --> 13:08.790
<i>Come on, Rush.
Go on, crush that Grog'.!</i>

13:09.540 --> 13:11.040
<i>If I can't change you, Dad,</i>

13:11.210 --> 13:12.960
<i>the Ultimate Prize will.</i>

13:13.630 --> 13:15.210
<i>I'm going to win this race.</i>

13:15.380 --> 13:17.090
<i>And I'll make her return.
You'll see.</i>

13:18.090 --> 13:22.760
<i>We'll be together
again... you, me, mother.</i>

13:23.390 --> 13:24.970
<i>Just like before.</i>

14:13.270 --> 14:16.110
You have come
seeking help, human.

14:16.520 --> 14:19.110
Yes. Are you the shaman?

14:19.400 --> 14:23.530
You have come to seek help
for a friend. A girl.

14:23.700 --> 14:25.570
Her name is Eva.

14:25.780 --> 14:27.870
Her name is Molly, actually.

14:28.030 --> 14:29.700
Though maybe it's not.

14:29.870 --> 14:31.830
How does this work exactly?

14:32.250 --> 14:36.790
Why don't you start by giving me
the stone in your pocket.

14:37.710 --> 14:39.880
What can you tell me
about this symbol?

14:42.050 --> 14:44.630
There is a great evil near this.

14:49.470 --> 14:51.470
This is a most dangerous request.

14:51.680 --> 14:55.270
Are you sure you are willing
to pay the price of knowledge?

14:55.560 --> 14:57.440
Yes, I'm ready.

14:58.520 --> 15:00.980
That thing sabotaged my ship.

15:01.570 --> 15:03.990
Molly... Eva,
whatever her name is,

15:04.150 --> 15:06.030
she might be the next target.

15:06.320 --> 15:09.580
The Ultimate Prize
arouses great envy.

15:09.740 --> 15:14.080
There are some that will stop
at nothing to possess its power.

15:17.080 --> 15:18.460
Give me your hand.

15:18.630 --> 15:21.210
I will make you see
the one you seek.

15:37.270 --> 15:38.900
What's happening to me?

15:47.410 --> 15:49.280
Sorgonic metal!

15:49.450 --> 15:51.660
I thought we took
all that from Byrus.

15:56.620 --> 15:58.710
Finally, the Crog
gets taught a lesson.

16:00.590 --> 16:02.420
You cannot beat me, Toros.

16:03.050 --> 16:04.550
I am never alone.

16:04.840 --> 16:07.090
All of Byrus flies with me.

16:07.510 --> 16:08.840
Thanks to the Crogs,

16:09.010 --> 16:11.470
civilization came
to your pitiful planet.

16:11.890 --> 16:15.480
The Crogs polluted our rivers
and destroyed our cities.

16:15.640 --> 16:17.060
You left nothing.

16:17.480 --> 16:19.310
Once I win the Ultimate Prize,

16:19.480 --> 16:21.560
all of your wrongdoing
shall be erased.

16:22.400 --> 16:23.770
Did anyone inform you

16:23.940 --> 16:27.240
that it was I who led
the Crog forces on Byrus?

16:27.860 --> 16:30.740
You? No. That's impossible.

16:37.910 --> 16:40.290
Look. What's he doing?
He had the advantage.

16:40.830 --> 16:42.460
Rush, don't do it.

16:43.960 --> 16:46.460
Forgive me, my brothers.
Forgive me.

16:46.630 --> 16:48.300
But I cannot let him go free.

16:48.590 --> 16:51.970
Your peace-loving people
did nothing to defend themselves.

16:52.140 --> 16:54.220
And you will do the same.

16:54.680 --> 16:58.060
<i>For... Byrus!</i>

17:04.190 --> 17:06.940
Come out, Toros,
and fight like a man!

17:07.190 --> 17:08.400
If you know how.

17:08.900 --> 17:11.660
You've made
your last mistake.

17:22.540 --> 17:23.290
Rush, no!

17:35.180 --> 17:36.760
Where am I?

17:36.930 --> 17:40.310
In my den.
You summoned me.

17:40.520 --> 17:42.850
Who? Who's talking to me?

17:45.360 --> 17:47.440
I go by many names.

17:51.450 --> 17:54.240
I am the Lord of Purity

17:54.410 --> 17:57.830
who tolerates no deviation.

18:01.870 --> 18:07.550
I am Canaletto, removed
from his rightful throne.

18:11.470 --> 18:13.590
I am the Timeless One

18:13.760 --> 18:18.060
<i>waiting to bring the old world
to its end.</i>

18:23.850 --> 18:25.060
You're mad!

18:25.230 --> 18:26.860
Stay away.

18:27.020 --> 18:28.360
Stay away from us!

18:28.570 --> 18:31.490
Who are you to command me?

18:31.650 --> 18:36.240
You're nothing but a pathetic pawn
in a game of my own design.

18:37.660 --> 18:39.790
Now, be gone.

18:40.620 --> 18:43.960
You are no longer of use to me.

19:10.270 --> 19:12.990
Rush? Rush?
Can you hear me?

19:13.570 --> 19:15.110
-Rush!
-Rush?

19:18.910 --> 19:21.040
Hang on, Rush.
We're going to get you out.

19:27.380 --> 19:29.250
That was quite a show, wasn't it?

19:31.750 --> 19:33.170
You were great today.

19:33.880 --> 19:35.630
Don't talk, just rest.

19:38.430 --> 19:40.600
The competition is over for me.

19:41.510 --> 19:45.390
I failed my mission
and my people.

19:46.770 --> 19:48.940
Why did you want to win
the Ultimate Prize?

19:49.150 --> 19:52.440
The Crogs destroyed
my beautiful planet, Byrus.

19:52.610 --> 19:56.070
And I wanted to bring it back
to its former glory.

19:56.280 --> 19:59.950
Although I guess
what I truly wanted was revenge.

20:00.240 --> 20:01.280
Hang in there, buddy.

20:01.450 --> 20:04.120
If I win, Rush,
I'll restore your planet for you.

20:04.410 --> 20:07.830
You're a sweet girl, Molly.
But I can't accept.

20:08.000 --> 20:13.000
My people will find a way
to rebuild Byrus again someday.

20:13.170 --> 20:15.880
This is our problem to solve.

20:16.550 --> 20:21.470
To capture the Ultimate Prize,
your intent must be pure.

20:22.720 --> 20:24.640
Mine was not.

20:25.390 --> 20:26.390
We're all set.

20:27.600 --> 20:29.480
Draw strength from it.

20:29.810 --> 20:32.360
And bring back the Prize!

20:42.740 --> 20:44.830
Did you find
what you were seeking?

20:52.500 --> 20:54.380
<i>I can't remember.</i>

20:54.550 --> 20:56.760
<i>I can't remember a thing.</i>

21:06.020 --> 21:08.850
OK, shove off.
There's no time to lose.

21:10.600 --> 21:12.610
How can we ever repay you?

21:12.900 --> 21:15.940
Just win big time.
That's all we ask.

21:22.740 --> 21:24.990
Farewell, humans. Win big.

21:25.160 --> 21:26.700
Make us look good.
